A1. These are usually well canvased. ~ CAMPS
A6. What school-teachers should have. ~ CLASS
A11. After this you will see "The Judge." ~ ARREST
A12. There's a sting to this. ~ HORNET
A14. What Sitting Bull must have had. ~ SEAT
A15. There's much of this, Shakespeare said, about nothing. ~ ADO
A17. This is used as a rule. ~ CODE
A18. A difficult thing to keep on one's wife. ~ TAB
A19. The more you push this the slower you go. ~ BRAKE
A21. Extra pale. ~ WAN
A22. The lesser half—according to the better half. ~ IT
A23. The country is full of them. ~ FARMERS
A25. Preposition. ~ TO
A26. This goes down in Florida. ~ REALTY
A28. This goes down in Florida, too. ~ SUCKER
A30. Most campaign speeches. ~ ROT
A31. A deer girl. ~ DOE
A32. This is hot stuff. ~ TAMALE
A35. There's sorrow in the air. ~ DIRGES
A38. An abbreviated highway. ~ RD
A39. Where there's a will. ~ TESTATE
A41. A triller's note. ~ LA
A42. Unit of work. ~ ERG
A44. The goal of shopping excursions. ~ STORE
A45. An inmate of the bughouse. ~ BUG
A46. This man looked out for a rainy day. ~ NOAH
A48. This believes in all work and no play. ~ ANT
A49. To lose color. ~ FADE
A50. To assimilate. ~ DIGEST
A52. Avoids. ~ EVADES
A54. Tight. ~ TENSE
A55. One who proposes—does this. ~ DARES

D1. To originate. ~ CREATE
D2. This fellow has a lot of sand. ~ ARAB
D3. What Tunney and Dempsey did. ~ MET
D4. Abbreviated afterthought. ~ PS
D5. Full of stars. ~ STARRY
D6. Throttlers. ~ CHOKES
D7. An exclamation meaning "Look." ~ LO
D8. You'll find this in the best circles. ~ ARC
D9. This is cold in Alaska. ~ SNOW
D10. Serene and placid. ~ SEDATE
D11. Active. ~ ASTIR
D13. This man will go high. ~ TENOR
D16. This is always obstructing. ~ DAM
D19. Inevitable results when Greek meets Greek. ~ BATTLES
D20. Fully instructed. ~ ERUDITE
D23. What Channel swimmers do to keep up. ~ FLOAT
D24. The Yanks would have won if it wasn't for this. ~ SCORE
D27. Nice around a girl. ~ ARM
D29. Often tapped at Yale. ~ KEG
D32. Inclination in a particular direction. ~ TREND
D33. Dexterous. ~ ADROIT
D34. Property. ~ ESTATE
D35. Wounded by Cupid. ~ DARTED
D36. What the bachelor does. ~ ELUDES
